{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 21, :comments ["And Moshe said: Six hundred thousand, etc. — this must be interpreted along the lines of what I explained: לא יוכל העם לעלות אל הר סיני. So too here, Moshe was afraid of what the Holy One, blessed be He, said: ואכלו חדש ימים — and he also said: והיה לכם לזרא. He asked the Holy One, blessed be He: You said they would eat for a month's time — but שש מאות אלף רגלי — besides the women and the little ones, and surely all their sheep and all their cattle would not suffice them for a month's time, so how will you fulfill this thing?! Either You will consume them and a few will remain and be sustained for a month, since after all You said: והיה לכם לזרא?! Or You will perform miracles for them to bring them meat from another place."], :book :numbers, :voice :rashbam, :lang :en, :chapter 11, :notes {0 "Resolved הקדוש ברוך הוא and הקב״ה both as 'the Holy One, blessed be He' per the voice rules; both refer to God."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:49:59.157337020Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}